TRUTHFUL LABEL, added after execution: this neutralisation DOES NOT reproduce the pre-v8 state and
its `loadBearing: false` is an artifact of my stub, not a finding. Emptying a sighting's annotations
blinds limb 3 as well, so the six alias/branch vectors refused at RELATION_DIGEST_UNANNOTATED
instead of being admitted. The pre-v8 code held TWO notions at once - coverage inherited, retention
and residue direct - which a single stub over the coverage function cannot express. The field-vector
control did behave as intended (identical in both states), so the neutralisation was targeted, just
not at the right seam. Superseded by probe-v7-vs-v8-inherited-limbs.v1.py, which measures the same
nine vectors across the two ACTUAL retained source images instead of a monkeypatch.
